      "side": 1,
      "message": "PTAL. I also updated GrDawnGpu to use a read-only GrDawnBuffer in onReadPixels and fixed the mapping bug for read-only buffers so that they can immediately use the blocking map.\n\nNOTE: the new behavior for a read-only buffer is as follows:\n1. They are not mapped at creation.\n2. GrGpuBuffer::map() will use a blocking map and return the mapped pointer as it does on other platforms if the buffer is not mapped when it gets called.\n3. GrDawnBuffer::mapAsync handles read-only buffers correctly, so a caller can still use mapAsync and then call `GrGpuBuffer::map()` to get the mapped pointer in the callback if they want to avoid spinning.",
      "revId": "3a1e57e67f584ae717d8a1ad46faaa6d666dad73",
